<title>USA: U.S. Steel raising steel prices in May.</title>
<headline>U.S. Steel raising steel prices in May.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>A spokesman for USX-U.S. Steel Group said Wednesday the company will raise steel prices by about three percent effective with May 4 shipments.</p>
<p>The increase follows a price hike on Tuesday by LTV Corp.</p>
<p>The spokesman said hot-rolled sheet will increase by $10 per ton; cold-rolled sheet will rise by $12 to $15 per ton; and galvanized sheet will increase by $18 per ton.</p>
<p>-- ((Pittsburgh newsroom 412-471-7088))</p>
</text>
